{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Real-Time Audio Processing Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: ring buffer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import collections"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class RingBuffer:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, capacity):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.buf = collections.deque(maxlen=capacity)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def write(self, frame):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.buf.extend(frame)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def read(self, n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [self.buf.popleft() for _ in range(min(n, len(self.buf)))]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def level(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return len(self.buf)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Capacity determines max buffering latency. 32,000 samples at 16 kHz = 2 s."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: VAD gate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def simple_energy_vad(frame, threshold=0.01):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return sum(x * x for x in frame) / len(frame) > threshold ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Replace with Silero VAD in production:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "vad, _ = torch.hub.load(\"snakers4/silero-vad\", \"silero_vad\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "is_speech = vad(torch.tensor(frame), 16000).item() > 0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: streaming ASR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Parakeet-CTC-0.6B streaming via NeMo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from nemo.collections.asr.models import EncDecCTCModelBPE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "asr = EncDecCTCModelBPE.from_pretrained(\"nvidia/parakeet-ctc-0.6b\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# chunk_ms=320 ms, look_ahead_ms=80 ms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for chunk in audio_stream():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    partial_text = asr.transcribe_streaming(chunk)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(partial_text, end=\"\\r\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: interruption handler"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Dialog:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.tts_task = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def on_user_speech(self, frame):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if self.tts_task and not self.tts_task.done():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.tts_task.cancel()   # barge-in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # then feed to streaming ASR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def on_final_user_utterance(self, text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.tts_task = asyncio.create_task(self.reply(text))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    async def reply(self, text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        async for tts_chunk in llm_then_tts(text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            speaker.write(tts_chunk)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Hinges on async I/O and cancellable TTS streaming. WebRTC peerconnection.stop() on the audio track is the canonical way."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. Simulates a ring buffer + energy VAD; prints stage latencies for a fake 10-second stream.\n2. **Medium.** Using `sounddevice`, build a passthrough loop that processes your mic in 20 ms frames and prints VAD state at each frame.\n3. **Hard.** Build a full duplex echo test with `aiortc`: browser \u2192 WebRTC \u2192 Python \u2192 WebRTC \u2192 browser. Measure glass-to-glass latency with a 1 kHz pulse."
      ]
    }
